  "result": "I added `parseRange` and committed it as `109bcfd`. `npm run fast` passed: Biome, tsc, boundaries and the related tests.\n\nThe commit title has no task id, which the repo convention calls for. My brief didn't include one and I didn't want to invent one. If you give me the id, I can amend the title to end with `(<id>)`.\n\n- **Function:** `src/cli/range.ts` exports `parseRange(text)`, so `1-3,5` gives `[1, 2, 3, 5]`. It accepts spaces around numbers and dashes, and returns `[]` for empty text. It throws on malformed segments such as `a` or `1,,2`, and on descending ranges such as `3-1`.\n- **Tests:** `test/cli/range.test.ts` uses `node:test` and covers the cases above.\n- **Shard weight:** I added `test/cli/range.test.ts` to `scripts/lib/shard-weights.mjs` with a weight of 0.1. That value is my estimate, not a measured one.",
